---
// Beta entry → Blak is the home. The old 4-tile overview is gone; every feature is
// reachable from the bottom bar (Minit · Blak · Nexus) and the profile/account screen.
// Blak's own AppLayout gate handles the sign-in redirect.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <title>Blaksyd</title>
    <!--
      OAuth / magic-link returns the token in the URL hash (#access_token=…, implicit
      flow) or query (?code=…). This page only bounces to /beta/blak/, where AppLayout's
      Supabase client consumes the token — so the hash/query MUST be carried through.
      A bare location.replace('/beta/blak/') drops it: the session never forms and the
      gate sends the user back to the landing page (the reported mobile login bug, only
      visible on a fresh device with no cached session). Script runs before the
      meta-refresh fallback so the token survives whenever JS is on.
    -->
    <script>location.replace('/beta/blak/' + location.search + location.hash);</script>
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=/beta/blak/" />
  </head>
  <body></body>
</html>
